  "reconstruction": {
    "scope": "Specific Gardoš Tower connected exterior: native asymmetric rounded/rectangular brick base and pale plinth, stepped arched closed entry, projecting front loggia and curved open columned gallery, two smaller round turrets/capped roofs/finials, central round brick shaft with arched recessed closed glazing/projecting sills/vertical piers, pale head/cornice and closed steep dark roof/finial. Four existing shared brick/raw-stone/paint/window-grid graphs. No snow, visitors, signs/heraldry/photo atlas, furnished interior, separate fortress ruins or whole hill/platform.",
    "identityBasis": "Retained exact-QID OSMway403091486/native building35184775180318 identifies Gardoš Tower. Own anchor20.409737414,44.848316064/global heading0/native east-south. Retained high-resolution mapped outline controls the complete base; internal X[0.436277643518402,0.899812101366741]/Z[-0.899812101366741,0.436277643518402] axes retain its rounded eastern end and squared western entry/loggia. Ordinary front and opposite photographs identify the base/gallery/two turrets/main shaft. Fine entry/window allocation retains20degree/2m uncertainty rather than a surveyed facade orientation.",
    "heightBasis": "Retained Wikidata height36m has no qualifying dimension or reference URL. Native PMTiles has no qualified height. Visualization uses base/gallery floor10.6..11.2m, columned gallery to17.7m, smaller turret caps23..24.8m/finials25.4m, upper shaft30m/head30.4m, steep roof35.4m and main finial36m. Floor, aperture/corbel/pier/rail/roof condition and hidden reverse inventory are picture-led estimates; no measured floor count or conservation survey is claimed.",
    "terrainBasis": "Retain original6m standard Mapzen ground, native paths/roads/water and all independent fortress/neighborhood buildings. Replace only the tower shell. Bounded buried feet follow the retained tower outline; the gallery is supported by its base/columns, with no whole-hill mesh, broad terrain platform, flattening or ground/water cutout. Coarse DEM contact/nearby ruin and bank heights are not surveyed foundation/flood measurements.",
